  "packRuntimeLine": "TensorRT 11.0.0.114 / CUDA 13.2.75 (measured, not inferred: the pack's own trtexec.exe reports TensorRT v110000 b114 and --getPlanVersionOnly on a plan it built reports version 11.0.0.114; its cudart64_13.dll is CUDART64_132_75.DLL 6,14,11,13020)",
  "ownedSdkLine": "TensorRT 11.3.0.99 / CUDA 13.4.92",
  "compatibility": "Measured boundary, not a general approval. The official 11.0.0.114 / CUDA 13.2.75 pack builds and runs only as its OWN matched runtime + SM120 builder-resource pair on the RTX 5090 (compute capability 12.0, driver 616.92 UNCHANGED by this work): engine build PASSED and real GPU inference PASSED. It is NOT equivalent to the owned TensorRT 11.3.0.99 / CUDA 13.4.92 SDK, which is newer. Cross-closure mixing is measured-incompatible: serialized engines fail to deserialize in BOTH directions (serialization version 243 vs 244) and cross-paired builder resources fail validateCaskKLibSize, so only a same-release pairing works. Do NOT install a mixed closure. A PTX-only closure (the six matched runtime files + nvinfer_builder_resource_ptx_11.dll, no SM resource) also FAILS at createInferBuilder (Unable to load library: nvinfer_builder_resource_sm120_11.dll: 126): the PTX resource does not substitute for the SM120 resource, and this release does not fall through to PTX-only on SM 120. Full evidence: native/videojanai-acquisition.md.",
  "rifeComparison": "All four exact v4.14 graphs match existing owned bytes. Weight-data lineage is ESTABLISHED by direct comparison: 128/128 initializer names and shapes with FP32->FP16 round-to-nearest-even bytes identical against the author's own MIT v4.14 / v4.14.lite checkpoints. Still unresolved: which exporter produced these files, the non-weight graph material, and the rights basis for redistributing the graphs as whole artefacts. Not executed; not a Ready capability.",
